command
Usage: command [-p] [-v|-V] NAME [ARGS]

Run NAME as a command, ignoring any shell function or alias of the same
name. With -v it does not run anything, it just says what would run.

	-v	print the path or the word "builtin"
	-V	the same, in a longer sentence
	-p	use a safe default PATH rather than yours

	command -v ls		is ls available, and what is it
	command ls		run the real ls, not an alias

`command -v` is the portable way to test whether something exists -- more
reliable than `which`, because it also knows about builtins.

See also: type, which, hash
